# --- s064 Book I d.26 q.1 (pp. 101–102)
n("n1155","s064-01","vtrum persone diuine constituantur in esse personali per relationes originis","la","source","Scotus, *Ord.* I d. 26 q. un. (*Utrum personae divinae constituantur in esse personali per relationes originis*; Wadding text checked locally).","verified")
n("n1156","s064-01","secundum Ricardum","la","source","*substantia* belongs to Boethius’ definition (*rationalis naturae individua substantia*); Richard of St Victor (*De Trin.* IV 21–22) rejects it in favour of *existentia*. The attribution to Richard reflects the conflation already seen in n945.","to-verify")
n("n1157","s064-01","relatio multiplicat trinitatem","la","source","Boethius, *De Trin.* 6: *substantia continet unitatem, relatio multiplicat trinitatem*; cited in *Ord.* I d. 26.","verified")
n("n1158","s064-01","quidquid est ad se est omnibus commune","la","source","Augustine, *De Trin.* V 8.9 (*quidquid ad se dicitur*), as cited in *Ord.* I d. 26.","probable")
n("n1159","s064-02","propositiui","la","historical","Praepositinus of Cremona († c. 1210). Cf. *Ord.* I d. 26: *opinio … Praepositivi, quod personae seipsis distinguuntur* (Wadding, checked locally).","verified")
n("n1160","s064-02","se totis distingui","la","textual","B: *se totum distingui*. B checked.","certain")
n("n1161","s064-02","Henrici predicatoris","la","historical","‘Henry the Preacher’, i.e. a Dominican Henry. Not identified; perhaps a confusion with Henry of Ghent, whose arguments against Praepositinus Scotus reports.","uncertain")
n("n1162","s064-02","q. ⟨39⟩","la","source","A (reading not quite clear) and B (*q. xxxix. ar. ii*) both cite q. 39 a. 2. The locus is Aquinas, *ST* I q. 40 a. 2 (*utrum relationes distinguant et constituant personas*), which is also the locus Wadding gives. A and B share the error. B checked.","verified")
n("n1163","s064-02","frater Johannes de Rippis","la","historical","John of Ripa OFM (fl. 1350s), *Lectura in I Sent.* and *Quodlibet*. The numbers *26* and *25* (B *xxvi. et xxv.*) have not been checked.","to-verify")
n("n1164","s064-02","sancti Johannis bonauenture","la","historical","Bonaventure was canonised by Sixtus IV on 14 April 1482, four years before this edition; hence *sanctus*. Locus: Bonaventure, *In I Sent.* d. 25 a. 1 q. 1? (not checked). B omits *Johannis*. B checked.","to-verify")
n("n1165","s064-02","vt Johannes Johanne inuetur","la","textual","*inuetur* gives no sense; read *iuuetur* (‘so that John [of Ripa] may be helped by John [Bonaventure]’), a pun. B: *vt iohannes inuere videatur in principio suo dist. xxv. q. i.*, also corrupt. B checked.","conjecture")
n("n1166","s064-03","opinio magistri","la","source","Whether Lombard himself (cf. *Sent.* I d. 26 c. 2–3) or the *magister* Praepositinus is meant has not been determined.","to-verify")
n("n1167","s064-03","persone trinitatis","la","textual","B: *persone in diuinis*. B checked.","certain")
n("n1168","s064-03","Est opinio doctoris et vera","la","doctrinal","In *Ord.* I d. 26 Scotus treats the view that the persons are constituted by something absolute as probable and does not condemn it; Gorris’s ‘the opinion of the Doctor, and the true one’ simplifies.","probable")
n("n1169","s064-03","Non est audendum vel cogitandum","la","source","Ps.-Dionysius, *De div. nom.* I 1 (Latin translations: *non audendum … dicere aut cogitare praeter ea quae nobis divinitus ex sacris eloquiis sunt expressa*). B: *Non est credendum*, an error. B checked.","verified")
n("n1170","s064-03","scilicet pater verbum et spiritus sanctus","la","intertext","1 Jn 5:7. B: *pater et filius et spiritus sanctus*. B checked.","certain")
n("n1171","s064-03","Anselmi de processu spiritus sancti","la","source","Anselm, *De processione Spiritus sancti* 1: *ubi non obviat aliqua relationis oppositio*.","verified")
n("n1172","s064-05","Sed aliquis quereret","la","textual","B: *Sed alias quereret*. B checked.","certain")
n("n1173","s064-05","insistens","la","commentary","*insistens*/*assistens*: the terminology goes back to Gilbert of Poitiers (relations as *assistentes*, not inhering), discussed by Bonaventure and Scotus. Exact source not checked.","to-verify")
n("n1174","s064-02","so that John may be helped by John","en","translation","Reading *iuuetur* for A’s *inuetur*; see the Latin note.")
